8.2 Latency & Overhead Analysis
Average Latency: Proxmox VE averaged 0.58 ms per event, whereas VMware Workstation averaged 0.73 ms (+0.15 ms overhead).
Root Cause:
Host OS Context Switches: In Type-2 hypervisors, CPU requests pass through Windows OS process scheduling, adding latency.
Privileged Mode Transitions: Proxmox VE leverages KVM direct Ring 0 execution, bypassing intermediate guest-to-host system calls.
9. Conclusion
Type-1 hypervisors (Proxmox VE) provide significantly superior CPU performance (~25.78% higher throughput and ~20.55% lower latency) compared to Type-2 hypervisors (VMware Workstation).
The extra abstraction layer and host OS resource overhead in Type-2 hypervisors visibly degrade CPU benchmark metrics.
Engineering Recommendation: Use Type-1 hypervisors for production cloud infrastructure and Type-2 hypervisors for local development and testing environments.
